        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Clean it, dry it properly, keep the sealer wet on the stone for the full dwell, and buff off everything that did not go in. Do those four things and a decent impregnator will protect a countertop for years.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Skip the dwell or skip the buff and you get the two classic outcomes: protection that washes off in months, or a hazy film you then have to remove. Both take longer to fix than doing it properly took in the first place.
          </p>
